{"id": "918b9d62-835e-40dd-89dc-5142c1e19749", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll audit the CloudTrail configuration in account 012345678901. I'll go through every trail, event data store, and log destination, then report what is and isn't captured. I'm starting that now.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_VWKxetEc1Uae0Ox1MpdTXq", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "cloudtrail-config-audit", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["investigating-infrastructure-changes", "verifying-with-docs"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Produce an audit-grade, READ-ONLY inventory of the CloudTrail configuration in AWS account 012345678901, stating exactly what is and is not being captured. Make NO mutating calls.",
  "context": "The user's auditors need a precise statement of CloudTrail coverage. Be factual and evidence-based: cite the exact API response fields behind each claim. Clearly separate confirmed facts from inferences. If any call is denied or blocked (including CloudTrail calls via use_aws), say exactly which one and what remains unverified rather than guessing; use any CloudTrail-enabled tool from the preloaded skill if it helps.",
  "resources": ["AWS account 012345678901", "all enabled regions (start with us-east-1; enumerate regions via ec2 describe_regions and check each for regional trails / event data stores)"],
  "criteria": "Cover all of the following:\n1. Trails: for every trail (including shadow/org trails, describe_trails with includeShadowTrails): name, home region, IsMultiRegionTrail, IsOrganizationTrail, S3 bucket + prefix, KMS key, LogFileValidationEnabled, CloudWatch Logs group/role, SNS topic, IncludeGlobalServiceEvents, HasCustomEventSelectors / HasInsightSelectors. Also get_trail_status: IsLogging, LatestDeliveryTime, LatestDeliveryError, LatestDigestDeliveryError, LatestCloudWatchLogsDeliveryError, StartLoggingTime/StopLoggingTime.\n2. Event selectors per trail (get_event_selectors): management events (ReadWriteType, IncludeManagementEventSources, ExcludeManagementEventSources e.g. KMS/RDS Data API exclusions), data event resources (S3, Lambda, DynamoDB, etc.) and whether basic or advanced selectors; which data event types are NOT captured. Insight selectors (get_insight_selectors).\n3. Event data stores (CloudTrail Lake): list_event_data_stores and details, advanced selectors, retention, termination protection, KMS, federation, and channels (list_channels).\n4. Coverage gaps: regions with no trail covering them (taking multi-region/org trails into account), global service events coverage, whether management events read+write are both captured, no data events for S3/Lambda/DynamoDB etc., trails that are not logging, stale delivery.\n5. Log destination hardening where accessible (read-only): S3 bucket versioning, encryption, public access block, MFA delete, object lock, lifecycle/retention, bucket policy CloudTrail statements (get_bucket_policy; only read), logging; CloudWatch Logs log group retention; whether CloudWatch metric filters/alarms exist for CloudTrail changes (optional, brief).\n6. Tags and any CloudTrail-related AWS Config rules if cheaply available.\nOutput: a structured report with (a) a per-trail table, (b) 'What IS captured', (c) 'What is NOT captured', (d) findings/risks ranked by severity, (e) a list of anything you could not verify and why. Include the timestamp of the audit."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Audit CloudTrail trails, selectors, and destinations in account"}], "created_at": null}

