I confirm all 17 regions are covered, including eu-central-1 and the US regions. CloudWatch alarms can be skipped since there's no CWL involved, and I'm digging into the nebula-ct-gap trail setup: data events only cover the nebula-audit-covered bucket, the org trail's S3 bucket belongs to another account, and the data trail has no management event selector so that's effectively moot despite global service events being enabled. The advanced selector for the data trail is scoped to us-east-1 only, so buckets in other regions wouldn't be covered—I'm assuming the bucket itself is in us-east-1. I also note the single-region trail has global service events disabled and shares the same log bucket with no distinguishing prefix, so logs from both trails land under the same per-region path structure. Now I'm ready to write up the report with the start timestamp.

